        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "80318c1a-49b0-39eb-a79f-ddc18c61fdae",
                "word": "cantharide",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7d8d0cee-be5c-4483-a1d5-cfcf0178fd46",
                        "entry_id": "80318c1a-49b0-39eb-a79f-ddc18c61fdae",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cantharides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                        "entry_id": "80318c1a-49b0-39eb-a79f-ddc18c61fdae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Coléoptère qu’on desséchait et réduisait en une poudre et qui servait surtout en pharmacie pour la préparation des vésicatoires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69c366c9-f6ab-4cd2-b272-e53e20a2f91e",
                                "sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                                "text": "Mais, par un raffinement de perversité incroyable, il avait glissé dans le dessert certaines pastilles de chocolat préparées avec des mouches cantharides. L'on connaît la vertu de ce médicament. Elle s'est trouvée telle que tous ceux qui en ont mangé se sont livrés à tous les excès auxquels porte la fureur la plus amoureuse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39bf3eda-1083-4005-8db9-3575e4de7957",
                                "sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                                "text": "Non, toutes ces étincelantes cantharides qu’on voit vibrer autour d’un frêne, dans l’or du couchant, personne n’en saurait extraire de philtre tel que la jalousie. Cela réveillerait les morts : cela les réveille peut-être ; et c’est alors que leur veuve en voit passer l’épouvante à travers son lit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aed3fc61-3ac1-4b0b-abe0-6adc12fe6075",
                                "sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                                "text": "Sébastien Chambot […] qui récolte des paquets de billets de mille avec des romans alambiqués et voluptueux, où il n'est question que de tortillements de la viande humaine saturée de cantharide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a529dd20-e91c-431b-bc72-eb99c5f51942",
                                "sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                                "text": "En fait, ce qui s’était passé (et c’est, paraît-il, chose fréquente), c’est que les cailles avaient croisé le nuage d’une migration de mouches cantharides, et en étaient gorgées. Bander est agréable, mais bander pendant deux jours, c’est atroce !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6d6262bd-423a-4a5e-9446-aade0ecacfbb",
                        "source_entry_id": "80318c1a-49b0-39eb-a79f-ddc18c61fdae",
                        "source_sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                        "target_lang_word": "Spanish fly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Spanish fly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b319a3f-2e1b-32a9-b3ec-7002a007d9ae",
                                        "entry_id": "db6b4b09-3684-3568-828a-c61541c4e522",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supposed aphrodisiac extracted from the beetle Lytta vesicatoria; cantharidin, the active ingredient, a vesicant used as a defence by L. vesicatoria and other blister beetles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f29032f9-4961-4530-8542-66d84612dd4c",
                                                "sense_id": "0b319a3f-2e1b-32a9-b3ec-7002a007d9ae",
                                                "text": "2010, Carol Turkington, Deborah R. Mitchell, cantharidin, entry in Encyclopaedia of Poisons and Antidotes, 3rd Edition, page 49,\nIngestion of Spanish fly causes burning in the throat and sloughing of the upper gastrointestinal tract."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c94ad9be-058c-4e93-ac22-79bd93b66b24",
                                                "sense_id": "0b319a3f-2e1b-32a9-b3ec-7002a007d9ae",
                                                "text": "The best-known aphrodisiac is Spanish fly, which is made from the wings of the blister beetle. Spanish fly creates a condition known as priapism in men. This is long-standing erection, which sounds good in theory. Unfortunately, Spanish fly removes all sensitivity from the organ, rendering it ineffective. In women the results are more severe. These include depression, vomiting, inflammation of the kidneys, and even death."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5305b13-decb-300a-b3f1-7920ea657cfc",
                                        "entry_id": "db6b4b09-3684-3568-828a-c61541c4e522",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The beetle Lytta vesicatoria."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38bda128-8b62-4001-9029-2dd9e75eabcd",
                                                "sense_id": "f5305b13-decb-300a-b3f1-7920ea657cfc",
                                                "text": "The Spanish''' fly abounds in the south of France, Spain, and Italy, and is found on the ash, lilac, privet, elder, honeysuckle, plum, willow, and elm trees.[…]The American fly is rather smaller than the Spanish fly, and of a much darker color."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0a99542-e66f-4fcc-9942-8ac09df6c891",
                                                "sense_id": "f5305b13-decb-300a-b3f1-7920ea657cfc",
                                                "text": "Spanish flies applied to the skin produce blisters (vesication, with inflammation and even sloughing)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c6c7994-dc91-41c7-b3f4-9a6bc7a9e573",
                        "source_entry_id": "80318c1a-49b0-39eb-a79f-ddc18c61fdae",
                        "source_sense_id": "cc167530-e685-3179-8c02-305f1981bc7b",
                        "target_lang_word": "cantárida",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cantárida",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cdddc6ce-35d5-3cd6-9b25-c0e930a7776b",
                                        "entry_id": "03e451c0-9d28-3588-a38c-247be037608b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(Lytta vesivatoria) Insecto coleóptero, de 15 a 20 milímetros de largo y de color oscuro brillante, que vive en las ramas de los tilos y, sobre todo, en los fresnos. Se emplea en medicina como vejigatorio, así en polvo como tintura alcohólica, en ungüento y emplasto y en papel apispástico."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3262e38-3eb8-4a21-915f-699a9078b767",
                                                "sense_id": "cdddc6ce-35d5-3cd6-9b25-c0e930a7776b",
                                                "text": "«Para el dolor de dientes existía una receta con la misma cantárida mezclada con opiáceos»."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d1ac54d-ca57-4e13-a974-fe0126123eed",
                                                "sense_id": "cdddc6ce-35d5-3cd6-9b25-c0e930a7776b",
                                                "text": "«A veces, recordaba la mirada de una mujer o el color de sus ojos y los asociaba al color de las cantáridas que permanecían inmóviles en sus cajas de cristal, atravesadas por un delgado alfiler de plata»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "deb2f40f-381b-386c-80b3-09e9e83406da",
                                        "entry_id": "03e451c0-9d28-3588-a38c-247be037608b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parche de cantárida₁ que se aplica a los enfermos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85b3c3b2-bd38-32c8-bc5b-dc5f12dbe4fe",
                                        "entry_id": "03e451c0-9d28-3588-a38c-247be037608b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ampolla o llaga que producen las cantáridas₁ sobre la piel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "596a75dc-7656-4baa-8330-822b72f99134",
                                                "sense_id": "85b3c3b2-bd38-32c8-bc5b-dc5f12dbe4fe",
                                                "text": "«Le han curado las cantáridas»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
